From: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: disable MAC EEE capabilities on EN7581

Stock AN7581 eth_ephy clears MDIO_AN_EEE_ADV (0x7:0x3c = 0) in
normalinit() and disables LPI on internal GSW ports. Match ID_EN7528 in
mt753x_phylink_get_caps() by leaving lpi_capabilities and
lpi_interfaces empty on ID_EN7581 so phylink keeps MAC LPI disabled and
rejects enabling EEE from userspace.

Signed-off-by: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -3112,13 +3112,13 @@ static void mt753x_phylink_get_caps(stru
 
 	priv->info->mac_port_get_caps(ds, port, config);
 
-	/* The EN7528 GPHYs report EEE capability, but negotiating EEE with
-	 * common link partners (e.g. Realtek GbE NICs) results in an unstable
-	 * link with dropped frames. Leave the LPI capabilities empty so that
+	/* The EN7528 and EN7581 GPHYs report EEE capability, but negotiating
+	 * EEE with common link partners (e.g. Realtek GbE NICs) results in an
+	 * unstable link with dropped frames. Leave LPI capabilities empty so
 	 * phylink disables EEE on these PHYs and refuses to enable it from
 	 * userspace.
 	 */
-	if (priv->id != ID_EN7528 &&
+	if (priv->id != ID_EN7528 && priv->id != ID_EN7581 &&
 	    config->mac_capabilities & (MAC_100FD | MAC_1000FD)) {
 		u32 eeecr = mt7530_read(priv, MT753X_PMEEECR_P(port));
 
